[15.407803, "o", "space;\r\n    31\t   • each output line consists of the join field, the remaining fields\r\n    32\t     from FILE1, then the remaining fields from FILE2.\r\n    33\t\r\n    34\t* Menu:\r\n    35\t\r\n    36\t* General options in join::      Options which affect general program behavior.\r\n    37\t* Sorting files for join::       Using ‘sort’ before ‘join’.\r\n    38\t* Working with fields::          Joining on different fields.\r\n    39\t* Paired and unpaired lines::    Controlling ‘join’’s field matching.\r\n    40\t* Header lines::                 Working with header lines in files.\r\n    41\t* Set operations::               Union, Intersection and Difference of files.\r\n    42\t\r\n    43\t8.3.1 General options\r\n    44\t---------------------\r\n    45\t\r\n    46\tThe program accepts the following options.  Also see *note Common\r\n    47\toptions::.\r\n    48\t\r\n    49\t‘-a FILE-NUMBER’\r\n    50\t     Print a line for each unpairable line in file FILE-NUMBER (either\r\n    51\t     ‘1’ or ‘2’), in addition to the normal output.\r\n"]
[15.407839, "o", "    52\t\r\n    53\t‘--check-order’\r\n    54\t     Fail with an error message if either input file is wrongly ordered.\r\n    55\t\r\n    56\t‘--nocheck-order’\r\n    57\t     Do not check that both input files are in sorted order.  This is\r\n    58\t     the default.\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\t‘-e STRING’\r\n    61\t     Replace those output fields that are missing in the input with\r\n    62\t     STRING.  I.e., missing fields specified with the ‘-12jo’ options.\r\n    63\t\r\n    64\t‘--header’\r\n    65\t     Treat the first line of each input file as a header line.  The\r\n    66\t     header lines will be joined and printed as the first output line.\r\n    67\t     If ‘-o’ is used to specify output format, the header line will be\r\n    68\t     printed according to the specified format.  The header lines will\r\n    69\t     not be checked for ordering even if ‘--check-order’ is specified.\r\n    70\t     Also if the header lines from each file do not match, the heading\r\n    71\t     fields from the first file will be used.\r\n    72"]
